🧩 Prompt Puzzle — Master AI Prompting Through Play
Day 35/60 — #60DaysOfClaudeAI
An interactive, single-file web app that teaches prompt engineering through gameplay instead of theory. Built entirely offline with zero dependencies — just open the HTML file.
🎯 What It Does
Prompt Puzzle turns the skill of writing good AI prompts into a hands-on game. Instead of reading tips about prompt engineering, you practice it — assembling, cleaning, and judging real prompts across coding-focused scenarios, then seeing exactly how a weak prompt vs. an optimized prompt vs. an over-engineered prompt would each perform.
🕹️ Three Challenge Types
Build the Prompt — drag or tap the right instruction blocks into place while avoiding distractor blocks that would weaken the output.
Clean the Prompt — a messy, noise-filled prompt is broken into lines; keep the useful ones and discard filler, flattery, and vagueness.
Choose the Best Prompt — pick which of three prompts (weak / optimized / over-engineered) will most reliably produce the desired output.
Every round ends with a full reveal: the weak prompt and its output, the optimized prompt and its output, the over-engineered version, and the underlying Prompt Principle behind the round.
📊 Live Scoring & Report
Tracks Accuracy, Time, Moves, Wrong Placements, Hints Used, and an Optimization Bonus in real time. At the end, a full Prompt Performance Report is generated:
Prompt Score (0–1000) and Rating (Novice → Prompt Architect)
A radar-style Prompt DNA visualization (Clarity, Context, Constraints, Format, Examples, Conciseness)
Personalized feedback on strengths and weak spots
A next milestone to chase
A reusable "ideal prompt template" built from your own session
🛠️ Tech Stack
Pure HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript — no frameworks, no CDNs, no build step. Fully self-contained in one file so it runs offline in any browser.
🚀 Run It
Download prompt-puzzle.html
Open it in any browser
Play through 6 randomized coding-focused scenarios
Replay anytime for a freshly shuffled set
📚 Domain & Difficulty
Currently configured for Coding & Tech at Intermediate difficulty. Scenario data is stored in a single reusable JavaScript array, so new domains or difficulty levels can be dropped in easily.
